From 831f188f3c76c5f642961c40bb3c9ff191d9bf66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:20:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 23/49] x86_64/fpu/587: use the generic expf, exp2f, logf,
 log2f and powf

2.27 replaced them by new flt-32 C implementations with new symbol
versions and no wrappers; the x87 versions only provide __ieee754_*f and
break the link (__expf).  i386 dropped its x87 versions the same way.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
---
 sysdeps/x86_64/fpu/587/e_exp2f.S |  50 -----
 sysdeps/x86_64/fpu/587/e_expf.S  |  55 -----
 sysdeps/x86_64/fpu/587/e_log2f.S |  66 ------
 sysdeps/x86_64/fpu/587/e_logf.S  |  68 ------
 sysdeps/x86_64/fpu/587/e_powf.S  | 365 -------------------------------
 5 files changed, 604 deletions(-)
 delete mode 100644 sysdeps/x86_64/fpu/587/e_exp2f.S
 delete mode 100644 sysdeps/x86_64/fpu/587/e_expf.S
 delete mode 100644 sysdeps/x86_64/fpu/587/e_log2f.S
